<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - S.Africa April retail sales up 0.2 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>TABLE - S.Africa April retail sales up 0.2 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African retail trade sales rose a seasonally adjusted 0.2 percent month-on-month in April to 11.94 billion rand, latest Central Statistical Service (CSS) data shows.</p>
<p>Year-on-year, seasonally adjusted retail sales were up 14.3 percent from 10.45 billion rand in April 1996, the CSS said.</p>
<p>On an actual basis, retail trade sales were up 2.4 percent month-on-month and up 14.3 percent year-on-year.</p>
<p>Retail trade sales at current prices.</p>
<p>(rand million):</p>
<p>				 Apr '97	 Mar '97	Apr '96</p>
<p>    Seasonally adjusted  11,942.2	11,916.3     10,448.8</p>
<p>    Actual		   11,577.5	11,301.9     10,131.6</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom, +27 11 482-1003</p>
